Package: rsiscorar
Title: Interface to the SISCORAR Tidal Current Prediction System
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R:
    person("Eduardo", "Leoni",
           email = "e.leoni@gmail.com",
           role = c("aut", "cre"),
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0003-0955-5232"))
Description: Predicts ocean currents for 5 Brazilian coastal bays using
    tidal harmonic analysis. The pure R path computes predictions at the
    ADCIRC computational mesh nodes (~3,000 per bay) using 13 independently
    fitted harmonic constituents, with no external dependencies.
    Optionally wraps the official SISCORAR executables (via Wine) for
    full 142-constituent output interpolated to a dense regular grid
    (~90,000 nodes). Exports to GRIB2, NetCDF, and GeoJSON formats for
    marine navigation software. SISCORAR is the Brazilian Navy's
    (DHN/REMO) adaptation of the ADCIRC finite-element coastal ocean model.
